+## Composer directory references
+
+This showcase stays dependency-free. In a Composer project, directory settings
+can refer to one another. For example:
+
+```json
+{
+  "config": {
+    "vendor-dir": "{$bin-dir}/packages",
+    "bin-dir": "tools with spaces"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Composer resolves the vendor directory to `tools with spaces/packages`. Its
+installed package metadata and generated autoload maps belong in that directory;
+completion and navigation read them there without executing PHP bootstrap files.
+The resolved setting can be checked with
+`composer --no-plugins --no-scripts config --absolute vendor-dir`.
+
+For an already installed project using this layout, generate optimized maps with
+`composer --no-plugins --no-scripts dump-autoload --no-dev --optimize`. The
+`none` indexing strategy still resolves classes listed in those maps and helpers
+listed in `autoload_files.php`; it does not scan missing classes into existence.
+
+Local references between `vendor-dir` and `bin-dir` are supported. Unknown,
+malformed, cyclic or over-budget references retain their explicit values rather
+than silently choosing the default vendor directory. This does not add global
+Composer configuration or environment-variable expansion.
